title: recent panel
tags: Panel [[Panel types]]
kind: reference
aliases: recently-viewed
summary: The metarecords you looked at last in this repository, newest first — as a panel, and as a pick from the command input.

A metarecord is ''viewed'' when `metarecord-detail` or the [[file panel]] shows it, and
a folder when the [[file-manager panel]] goes into it. The GUI keeps the last 200 of
each repository — and, beyond them, those viewed often ([[Frecent folders]]) — most
recent first, each once: viewing one again moves it to the front. The list is the GUI's — a file of the repository,
`.metafolder/gui/recent` — and no field of the metarecord: recording a view writes
nothing to the daemon, so it adds no write to the event log.

!! As a pick

<<key "recent other time" "g r">> (`recent <where> time`) lists them in the command
input, newest first, each as its path, its `label`, its `name` and its ''score'';
<<key "recent other score" "g m">> (`recent <where> score`) lists them best score
first. The score is the entry's number of views, aged, weighted by how recently it was
last viewed ([[Frecent folders]]), shown to one decimal. Type to narrow, `Enter` to open: the metarecord becomes
the selection and is shown in the ''other'' slot — in the [[file panel]] when it has a
file, in `metarecord-detail` otherwise ([[Cross-panel selection]]). The lines are
built by `recentLine` in the shipped `gui/commands.js` ([[User commands]]): change it
there to change what a line shows.

!! As a panel

Open it with `panel:open here recent` (<<key "panel:open here recent" "t v">>). One row
per metarecord: its `label`, else its `name`, else the start of its uuid; its path;
its score; how long ago it was viewed. The rows are newest first, or best score first
with ''sort'' in the toolbar or `recent:set sort score`; the choice is the
workspace's (`recent:sort`).

* <<key "cursor:next self" "↓ or j">> / <<key "cursor:prev self" "↑ or k">>, <<key "cursor:first self" Home>> / <<key "cursor:last self" End>> — move the cursor. The row under it is the workspace's selection, so a detail or file panel beside it follows.
* <<key "panel:open other file" "Enter or →">>, or the `↗` button of a row ([[Opening a row]]) — show it in the [[file panel]] of the other slot; <<key "panel:open other metarecord-detail" Shift+Enter>>, or the `ⓘ` button, in the [[metarecord-detail panel]]. After `b` in a new workspace, after `i` in place of this panel ([[open targets|Panel slots and layout]]).
* <<key "cursor:find self select" f>> — jump to a row by name; a candidate carries its path, which tells two rows of the same name apart ([[Jumping to an entry]]).
* <<key "recent:set sort" s>> — newest first ⇄ best score first (the question offers the other order).
* <<key "view:refresh self" r>> — read the list again.

The rows are a snapshot: they are read when the panel is shown, on a refresh and when
metarecords change, not at each view — walking the list does not reorder it under
the cursor, although each row walked is itself a view. A right click offers the
metarecord's actions and, when it has a file, the file's ([[Context menus]]).
